 A third registration, written after the four test sets of the Vietnamese and English arms had been decided, is the **Flickr30K comparison (Section 8.6)**: a same-data comparison with a re-implemented training-free baseline, LMCap, plus a third backbone. It follows a three-tier rule. Claims were nominated on a carve of Flickr30K train, rehearsed once on Flickr30K val, and taken to a one-look test only if the rehearsal passed with margin, that is, with a predicted probability of passing on test of at least 0.98. At test a claim passed if its point was at least +2.0 and its Holm-adjusted one-sided bootstrap statistic was below 0.05; that statistic is p-like, not an exact p-value (Section 8.6). The registration does not amend the test registration above.
 
